 F.22,"For the actual pro-5 tripod action over G_Q,{2,3,5}, every integral class-two section lifts to class three with a Z5²-torsor of lift classes, and every class-three section has exactly125 class-four lifts. Noncanonical section-set products are Z5^8 and Z5^8 times (Z/5)^3. The latter parameters are the explicit cocycle (chi^4-1)/5, persist under reduction, and disappear upon rationalization. The full and metabelian quotients agree through class four. All induced relative Fermat images and finite quotient counts are evaluated.",Proved,"sections/F_advanced.tex, Statement F.22 and proof; code/F_advanced_integral_layers.py/.json/.out","F.20; Milne2006 I.Corollary4.15 and II.Proposition2.9; Milne2020 ANT Theorems4.3,5.1,5.11; Weibel2013 IV.Corollary1.13, VI.§8.1.1, proof of Theorem8.2 and Table10.1.1; SGA1 XIII.Corollary2.9 and §2.10; Actual tangential action, central nonabelian cohomology, and twisted fixed-group calculation","C4 §51, f.734, scan173: successive approximations and splittings; C4 §51, f.736, scan178: inadequacy of the abelian approximation",No,"The integral central H1 groups in weights2,3,4 are0,Z5,Z/5 and H2 is zero. This is proved directly from the class-number-one cyclotomic field Q(zeta5), its three fixed S-primes, the trivial two-dimensional Brauer module, and the S-unit character decomposition1^3+omega+omega². Compact inverse limits and explicit H0(Q5/Z5(j)) recover the exact integral torsion. The actual nonlinear Ihara action is retained; only its central graded layers are diagonal. All twisted integral fixed groups vanish, so the displayed fibres are free torsors. Finite counts are5^(6r),5^(8r),5^(8r+3) at classes2,3,4. All-level relative Fermat descent is the full fibre above abelian zero, not just the distinguished section. Unrestricted ramification at classes3 or higher and the full global Alexander module remain open."
