+
+The three specified unit tangential cusp sections at0,1,infinity have identical integral pro-5 classes through class2, but are pairwise distinct in class3. The coefficient of the standard interval-path cocycle on the cyclotomic kernel is exactly κ3[X+Y,[X,Y]]/48 in the stated path convention. This follows from the direct polylogarithmic path formulas of Nakamura–Sakugawa–Wojtkowiak: log(f) has coefficient−li3, li3=tildeκ3/2, and tildeκ3=κ3/(1−5²). Their discussion explicitly applies over number fields and identifies the z=1 specialization with the raw Soulé character. The same normalization agrees with the independent Tate substitution in Nakamura's final2013 article. Reversing the transition path changes the leading sign without changing separation.
